From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: add an ethernet0 alias so U-Boot can set the MAC

Without an "ethernet0" entry in /aliases nothing hands the board's real MAC
address to the kernel, and stmmac falls back to a generated one. It is not
stable across probes -- three probes in one session on the same board produced
three different addresses. Every reboot looks like a new machine to the DHCP server and to anything keyed on the address.

U-Boot already knows the right one and prints it while starting
("Ethernet0 MAC address: ...").

It hands it over in fdt_fixup_ethernet(), which walks the /aliases node looking
for "ethernet%d" properties and writes mac-address / local-mac-address into each
referenced node from its ethaddr / eth%daddr environment. Our DT carried only
serial0, so the loop found nothing to fix up and the kernel was left to invent
an address.

Add the alias. This keeps the address where it belongs -- the board, not the DT
-- so nothing has to be hardcoded here and boards with different addresses stay
correct.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 	#size-cells = <2>;
 
 	aliases {
+		ethernet0 = &gmac0;
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 	};
 
